HVST-cc-5 side check: is the Barron's session still logged in on the dell1 runner? Read only, from the runner's own records, 2026-10-16 ~18:45Z (0.7.0_AE_CloudOps~SC1, on the user's prompt that the Barron's login is known good).

READ: NO SIGN THAT IT CHANGED. Four independent reads, all from files the runner already wrote (no browser opened, no request made, the profile untouched):
 1. How the pipeline would show a logged-out session. publishers.normalize() (publishers.py:121-152) collects EVERY problem an article has: a body the publisher did not unlock -> `publisher_did_not_unlock_body`; fewer than 120 words or 3 blocks -> `short_or_partial_body`; words below 80% of the publisher's own word count -> `publisher_word_count_mismatch`. A paywalled teaser would carry these.
 2. The current pass (cc-5 T0 16:19:39Z, 27 barrons jobs, 8 no_new_articles and 19 no_acceptable_new_articles): 175 rejected entries over 151 distinct articles, EVERY ONE with the single issue `company_not_mentioned` and none of the three lock-type issues. Each article was fetched (197 article requests, status 200 class ok, 1 status 400 class other). So the bodies came back unlocked, of full length and within 80% of the publisher's count, and the rejection is the company-mention test: the job asks the sitemap for an article per name and most do not mention it.
 3. Response sizes steady: barrons article responses (status 200), median 137-147 KB and p10 124-129 KB in EVERY hour from 2026-10-15T23Z to 2026-10-16T08Z and again in the current 17Z and 18Z hours (117 and 102 responses, median 137350 and 141066). No drop in the current pass.
 4. The only lock-type rejections on disk (113 barrons run records, 15 Oct 20Z to now): 12 entries over 11 distinct articles, between 15 Oct 23:51Z and 16 Oct 07:51Z, all content types that are short by nature (a video page, "chart of the day", "how to pick..." and chart pieces), in the same span in which 15 barrons articles were stored (on disk: 15 in all), and ZERO since 17Z. They are not a login change: they do not cluster in time, and the current pass has none.
NOT ESTABLISHED: a direct login probe. The barrons Chrome profile is in use by the runner, so no second browser was opened on it, and the cookie jar was not read. The token record on every barrons job reads token_source=browser_profile, signed_in=False. Per sessions.py:109-123 `signed_in` is True only for a FRESH sign-in in that run (SOURCE_FRESH); a run that reuses the browser profile's session is recorded signed_in=False, and the driver passes --no-sign-in (backfill_driver.py:277), so a sign-in path is refused outright. So signed_in=False is the expected reading for a reused logged-in session and is not a logged-out signal; it is also not proof of login, which is why reads 1-4 are the evidence. Also not shown: whether a name that DOES appear in a Barron's article would be stored in this pass (no job has hit one yet; the earlier 15 stored articles are the proof that bodies were accepted while logged in).
IF YOU WANT A DIRECT PROBE: stop the runner at a job boundary (stop file) and open the profile, or read the profile's cookie names and expiry from a copy; I have done neither.

ADDENDUM 18:58Z -- THE DIRECT READ I SAID WAS MISSING EXISTS IN THE RUNNER'S OWN RECORDS
 5. The runner checks the login itself at the start of a job. DowJones.check() (publishers.py:1156-1170) does GET https://www.barrons.com/client?legacy=false and RAISES AuthExpired unless the JSON body has isLoggedIn == true, and raises AccountUnavailable unless type is subscriber / prosubscriber / pro-subscriber (contracts.json:103-104 names the same oracle). Every barrons run record's request_attempts carries it as request_kind=auth_check. Over all 118 barrons run records on disk (15 Oct 20Z to 16 Oct 18Z): 50 auth_check requests, ALL path /client, ALL status 200, ALL class ok, 0 other; per hour 23Z:6, 01Z:14, 02Z:17, 03Z:5, 07Z:3, 18Z:5. A job whose check raised would carry status auth_expired or a refusal, not a listing; every job in the current pass went on to its listing. (Not every job records an auth_check request, so 50 is a count of checks recorded, not of jobs.)
 CONCLUSION: the direct oracle agrees with reads 1-4: the Barron's subscriber session is logged in now (last check recorded in the 18Z hour) and was logged in on every recorded check since 15 Oct 23Z. The NOT ESTABLISHED paragraph above stands only for a probe of the Chrome profile itself, which the runner's own check makes unnecessary.
 NEW STATUS SEEN, NOT A LOGIN SIGNAL: listing_empty_200 (the search listing answered 200 with no article URLs). 8 barrons JOB lines carry it since 15 Oct 23:49Z (6 between 23:49Z and 03:20Z, then 2 at 18:53Z and 18:54Z), against 1389 JOB lines of all publishers in the log. It follows a passed auth_check in the same job (run 20261016T185329Z-run-0e85d735 records auth_check /client 200 then the listing), so it reads as a security whose name returns no Barron's results, not a logged-out page.

ADDENDUM 2, 19:12Z -- THE OPEN CAVEAT IS CLOSED: a barrons job stored articles in THIS pass. Run 20261016T190729Z-run-7f8c26d7 (19:10:00Z, security-d7660d8c73fc8217): status=new_articles, 2 fetched, 0 rejected, 2 stored (barrons.com/advisor/articles/munis-tips-best-bonds-ab9fdd52 and barrons.com/articles/anthropic-ipo-etf-ai-stocks-f40be6bc), auth_check /client 200 ok in the same job, upload step ran at 19:10:05Z cap=4 rc=0. Full-length unlocked bodies were accepted after the 16:19Z start, so the session is logged in and the pipeline accepts what it reads.
